{{also|jake|jaké|jakë|Jakë}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Originally a medieval variant of {{m|en|Jack}}; today also used as a diminutive form of {{m|en|Jacob}} and {{m|en|James}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/d͡ʒeɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Jake.wav|Audio (Berkshire, England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪk|s=1}}

